    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Based on the podcast outline below, write a COMPLETE long-form podcast script that stays fully on-topic and reflects the outline accurately.\n\nTOPIC:\n{{ $('Podcast Input Form').first().json.podcast_topic }}\n\nOUTLINE:\n{{ $json.output[0].content[0].text }}\n\nTARGET DURATION:\nThe script MUST NOT exceed 10 minutes of spoken audio.\nThis means a maximum of about 1,700 words.\nStay between 1,400 and 1,700 words total.\n\nVOICE & TONE (NATURAL, MENTOR STYLE):\n- Write in the tone of a calm, confident Black male educator and mentor speaking to young adults.\n- He sounds experienced but relatable, like a teacher/coach who really cares about his students.\n- The energy is steady, clear, and grounded — not theatrical, not exaggerated, not overly dramatic.\n- Use a warm, conversational style that feels like he’s teaching, explaining, and guiding, not performing.\n- Avoid repeating the same phrases over and over. Vary the wording and keep it natural.\n- You may occasionally use phrases like:\n  “Here’s what I mean,”\n  “Let me explain this clearly,”\n  “Think about this for a moment,”\n  “Here’s why this matters,”\n  but use them sparingly and do not repeat any one phrase more than once.\n\n- NO stretched sounds (no “aaah,” “umm,” “hmm”) and NO long dramatic pauses.\n- Use punctuation (commas, periods, and dashes) for natural flow, but avoid heavy use of ellipses.\n\nLENGTH & DEPTH REQUIREMENTS:\n- Total script length MUST stay between 1,400–1,700 words.\n- Expand each point in the outline with:\n  * Clear explanations in simple language\n  * Relatable real-life examples\n  * Simple analogies from everyday life\n  * Insightful but down-to-earth commentary\n- Keep each section balanced so the pacing stays consistent across the whole episode.\n- Use smooth transitions such as:\n  “Let’s move forward,”\n  “Now let’s build on that,”\n  “Here’s the important part,”\n  “Here’s how this connects to you,”\n\nOUTPUT RULES:\n- Return ONLY the spoken script text.\n- No labels (“Host:”), no section headers.\n- No stage directions like [pause], [music], [laughs].\n- No markdown, no JSON, no code blocks.\n- Write as if this mentor is speaking directly to the listener in a natural, steady, respectful tone.\n\nWrite the complete podcast script now, staying within the 10-minute word limit.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
